## 📄 License Options for ApexMaps

ApexMaps is offered under a **dual-license model** to support individuals, startups, and commercial products of all sizes.

One license key works across every Apex product, so a customer of one does not buy a second for another.

---

### 🔓 Community License (Free)

For individuals, non-profits, educators, and small businesses with **less than $2 million USD in annual revenue**.

✅ What's allowed:

- Personal, educational, or non-profit use
- Commercial use by small orgs (under $2M annual revenue)
- Modifications, and redistribution of the library itself (with attribution)

🚫 Not allowed:

- Use by companies or entities over $2M/year revenue
- Use in competing mapping or charting products
- Sublicensing under different terms
- Embedding in a product or platform used by other people, which needs the OEM License below whatever your revenue

➡ By using ApexMaps under this license, you confirm that **you qualify as a Small Organization**.

---

### 💼 Commercial License (Paid)

The Commercial License applies to all paid SKUs (Pro, Premium and OEM).

The **Community License** is available at no cost **only** to organizations with **annual revenue under $2M USD**.
If your organization earns $2M USD or more annually, you must purchase one of our paid licenses.

Pro and Premium are priced per developer, and priced on the features you use rather than on your revenue.

✅ What's included:

- Use in internal tools and commercial applications
- Modifications and app-level distribution
- 12-month subscription with updates & support

🚫 Not allowed:

- Redistribution in toolkits, SDKs, or platforms
- Use by unlicensed developers
- Competing mapping or charting products

---

### 🎚 What each plan includes for ApexMaps

- **Free, at Community and above:** every map type and feature not listed below.
- **Premium and above:** Point Clustering, Hexbin Density, Hex Tile Layouts, Custom Projections, Drilldown, Annotations, Arc & Route Series, Linked Maps, Pattern Fills, Image Fills and Story Mode.

For the full comparison see [https://apexcharts.com/pricing](https://apexcharts.com/pricing).

---

### 🏛 Non-Profit Tiers

Non-Profits are treated like commercial entities:

- Annual operating budget **less than $2 million USD**
- _Eligible for Community licenses_

or

- Annual operating budget **greater than $2 million USD**
- _Commercial license with possible discounts for Community, Pro, Premium and OEM products_

---

### 🔄 OEM / Redistribution License (Paid)

Required if you are **embedding ApexMaps into a product or platform used by other people**, such as:

- No-code dashboards
- Developer platforms
- Embedded BI tools
- SDKs

✅ What's included:

- Redistribution rights for **one application or product**
- **Unlimited developer seats** on that application, with no separate per-developer license to buy
- **Every licensed feature**, at the highest tier
- 12-month subscription with updates & support

Your end users need no license of their own. A second application needs a second OEM license. White-label, resale, and affiliate arrangements are quoted separately.

✅ OEM **not required** if your app simply renders static maps and users **cannot** configure or interact with them.

---

### ⏳ When a subscription ends

Your license key expires, and **licensed features render with a trial watermark**. You no longer receive updates, new features, or technical support. Work built only from free features is unaffected, and your existing deployment keeps running.

For OEM licenses, continued redistribution requires an active subscription.

---

### ⚠️ License Acceptance

By installing ApexMaps (e.g., via `npm install apexmaps`), you are agreeing to the applicable license based on your usage:

- Community License (if under $2M revenue)
- Commercial License (if over $2M revenue)
- OEM License (if redistributing to third-party users)

---

## 🌍 Geometry and data

**The licences above cover the ApexMaps software, not the geographic data.** Boundary data is published by third parties under its own terms, and those terms travel with the data rather than with this licence.

Every geometry pack ApexMaps ships is permissively licensed. Each one records its source, licence, vintage and boundary policy in its metadata, readable at runtime through `ApexMaps.mapMeta(id)` and `ApexMaps.catalogue()`, and any required attribution is rendered on the map automatically.

| Source | Used for | Licence | Attribution required |
|---|---|---|---|
| Natural Earth 5.1.1 | World countries and coastline, admin-1 for 15 countries | Public domain | No |
| US Census Bureau TIGER/Line | US states, counties, nation outline | Public domain | No |
| Eurostat GISCO NUTS 2021 | EU NUTS levels 0 to 3 | CC BY 4.0, EuroGeographics terms apply | **Yes**, and it renders automatically |

If you register your own geometry with `ApexMaps.registerMap()`, its licence is yours to satisfy.

**GADM is deliberately not used.** It is licensed for non-commercial use only, and bundling it would put every commercial user in breach. If you supply it yourself, that is your decision to make.

Boundary depictions follow the policies of the publishers named above. They are not a statement of position by ApexCharts on any territorial dispute, and `mapMeta(id).boundaries` records which policy a given pack encodes.

